{:spec/title "A work spec whose run throws moves to work/failed instead of staying in work/in-progress"

 :spec/description
 "When `miniforge run` starts a spec that lives under `work/`,
  `ai.miniforge.cli.workflow-runner.spec-kanban/start-spec!` moves the file
  to `work/in-progress/`. When the run returns, `finish-spec!` moves it to
  `work/done/` or `work/failed/` by the result. Both calls sit in
  `run-workflow-from-spec!` in `bases/cli/src/ai/miniforge/cli/workflow_runner.clj`,
  but `finish-spec!` runs only on the normal return of
  `execution/execute-with-events`. When the run throws (for example a
  namespace that fails to load, as on 2026-11-05), the spec stays in
  `work/in-progress/`, the launching checkout is left with a tracked file
  deleted, and the next `bb dogfood` refuses to start on a dirty tree.
  Stale copies in `work/in-progress/` accumulated this way.

  Change: when the run throws after `start-spec!` moved the spec,
  `finish-spec!` (or the move it wraps) still runs and files the spec under
  `work/failed/`, then the exception propagates unchanged. A run whose spec
  is not under `work/` is unaffected."

 :spec/intent
 {:type :bugfix
  :scope ["bases/cli/src/ai/miniforge/cli/workflow_runner.clj"
          "bases/cli/src/ai/miniforge/cli/workflow_runner/spec_kanban.clj"
          "bases/cli/test/ai/miniforge/cli/workflow_runner/kanban_test.clj"]}

 :spec/constraints
 ["The original exception propagates unchanged; filing the spec must not replace or swallow it"
  "A failure to move the spec is reported on stderr and does not mask the run's exception"
  "Tests use a temp directory as the working tree; they never move files under the repository's work/"]

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 ["A run that throws after start-spec! leaves its spec in work/failed/, not work/in-progress/"
  "The exception the run threw is the exception the caller receives"
  "A run that returns normally still files its spec under work/done/ or work/failed/ by its result"
  "A spec outside work/ is not moved on either path"]

 :spec/priority
 {:tier :high
  :axes #{:correctness :dogfood-enabler}
  :theme :dogfood-resilience
  :rationale "A dogfood run that throws leaves the launching checkout dirty, so the next run refuses to start until someone restores the file by hand."
  :blocks []
  :blocked-by []}

 :spec/workflow-type :canonical-sdlc}
